{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2610 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "d6e8df80b3882f37d5633af7d79c49211b3beb351f3334a3908fcc9ff0630962" :edb/db-before-t 2609 :edb/db-after-t 2610 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535922 50 #inst "2026-10-09T10:42:25.447Z" 13194139535922 true] [17592186096382 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072055/assets/49df59f984403cbbc994361c96313eca4d0875a7030dd997c90f1e393e23b69c.png)\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139535922 true] [17592186096382 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y+z=1 \\\\ y+z=-2 \\\\ -x+2y+z=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139535922 false] [17592186096382 1145 "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y+z=1 \\\\ y+z=-2 \\\\ z=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=2$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+(2)=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=-4$ and $z=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(-4)+(2)=1\\,⟹\\,x=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-5,$ $y=-4,$ and $z=2.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -5,-4,2 \\rangle.$" 13194139535922 false] [17592186096382 1145 "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072055/assets/dded05f0961034de6808d8f91f64afe8c367cec3c11fafdb26946090fa9c0891.png)\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=2$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+(2)=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=-4$ and $z=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(-4)+(2)=1\\,⟹\\,x=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-5,$ $y=-4,$ and $z=2.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -5,-4,2 \\rangle.$" 13194139535922 true] [17592186096383 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x+y+z=-2 \\\\  & x+y+2z=-1 \\\\  & x+2y+z=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139535922 false] [17592186096383 1100 "Consider the system of linear equations\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072055/assets/0c3483f97994da22dc0c739f9c3a26f87e070d28b684e63955a1129d00f9c755.png)\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139535922 true] [17592186096383 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072055/assets/9f1beb75e17aabdbeb5d814ae7ce3018f2ea89c36211070d40060d57445ca936.png)\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get $a_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072055/assets/84de3f5eddf0a05d4f2d69aebd1537feb23a228fba3e1af31678dd4bdb1b59df.png)\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z,$ and the second equation $y=3$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting these values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+(3)+(1)=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-6,$ $y=3,$ and $z=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -6,3,1 \\rangle.$" 13194139535922 true] [17592186096383 1145 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get $a_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+z=-2 \\\\ y=3 \\\\ z=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z,$ and the second equation $y=3$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting these values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+(3)+(1)=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-6,$ $y=3,$ and $z=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -6,3,1 \\rangle.$" 13194139535922 false] [17592186096593 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374521 13194139535922 true] [17592186096593 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374535 13194139535922 true] [17592186096593 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374542 13194139535922 true] [17592186096593 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374549 13194139535922 true] [17592186096594 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374528 13194139535922 true] [17592186096594 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374556 13194139535922 true] [17592186096594 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374563 13194139535922 true] [17592186374521 1017 #edb/ref 17592186374522 13194139535922 true] [17592186374521 1089 "q-130926" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374521 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535922 true] [17592186374521 1100 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 3 & -9 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139535922 true] [17592186374521 1113 #uuid "431a8c5f-b48a-570a-b528-7d3773d13396" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374521 1145 "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & 3 & -9 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-2y+z=-3 \\\\  & y-2z=-2 \\\\  & z=8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=8$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-2(8)=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-2+16=14.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=14$ and $z=8$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2(14)+(8)=-3\\,⟹\\,x=17.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=17,y=14$, and $z=8.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨17,14,8⟩.$" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374522 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374523 13194139535922 true] [17592186374522 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374524 13194139535922 true] [17592186374522 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374525 13194139535922 true] [17592186374522 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374526 13194139535922 true] [17592186374522 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374527 13194139535922 true] [17592186374522 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535922 true] [17592186374522 1041 "selection" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374522 1104 #edb/ref 17592186374525 13194139535922 true] [17592186374522 1110 #uuid "1cdfc3bd-fdca-5559-ad69-5b8738763495" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374523 1034 "⟨5,6,4⟩" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374523 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535922 true] [17592186374523 1111 #uuid "3ebf0657-4d78-56b5-bc74-4d6bc0c5e774" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374524 1034 "⟨17,6,8⟩" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374524 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535922 true] [17592186374524 1111 #uuid "5e44dfbf-d02b-5a54-9aa0-a085019bdd61" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374525 1034 "⟨17,14,8⟩" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374525 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535922 true] [17592186374525 1111 #uuid "11707825-b7d1-526d-a0ca-83315a9b9953" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374526 1034 "⟨5,14,8⟩" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374526 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535922 true] [17592186374526 1111 #uuid "4d0fbf33-cdc4-5298-bc6b-877279fbd179" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374527 1034 "⟨-1,2,2⟩" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374527 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535922 true] [17592186374527 1111 #uuid "a34f2682-c1ea-5c34-9310-eb89c305ab31" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374528 1017 #edb/ref 17592186374529 13194139535922 true] [17592186374528 1089 "q-130928" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374528 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535922 true] [17592186374528 1100 "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -4 & -12 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." 13194139535922 true] [17592186374528 1113 #uuid "59d8291a-54d6-53ae-b0c1-56a672117493" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374528 1145 "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -4 & -12 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 10 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $2$nd row by $\\frac{1}{3}$ and the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{7}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{7}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{7}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374529 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374530 13194139535922 true] [17592186374529 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374531 13194139535922 true] [17592186374529 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374532 13194139535922 true] [17592186374529 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374533 13194139535922 true] [17592186374529 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374534 13194139535922 true] [17592186374529 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535922 true] [17592186374529 1041 "selection" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374529 1104 #edb/ref 17592186374530 13194139535922 true] [17592186374529 1110 #uuid "59ced7c4-89a1-5c1d-b82e-60536562e135" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374530 1034 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{7}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374530 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535922 true] [17592186374530 1111 #uuid "84826572-6121-5e20-abb0-c418ae03d84c" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374531 1034 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 14 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & \\frac{3}{7}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374531 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535922 true] [17592186374531 1111 #uuid "1a6e9369-3da4-5641-a4c0-d99cd4fac697" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374532 1034 "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{7}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535922 true] [17592186374532 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535922 true] [